---
arrangement: whylog-corrupt-results-block-overruns
---
-- .whylog --
dorc-whylog/2 nonce=dorc attempt=0 host=fixture target=width-one generation=width-one mode=plan started=- @@dorc@@
results bytes=9999

-- replay --
$ dorc why --last --whylog=.whylog
whylog: warning[whylog-corrupt]: the saved why-log is damaged and cannot be read
back (results block byte-count exceeds the file)
   = help:  this usually means an interrupted write; re-run `dorc why` live, and
            the next plan or apply will save a fresh why-log
